armacraft perf patch 0004 -- UNAPPLIED. Protocol feature `delta` (host side). Pairs with 0003.

What it does:
- Msg.Hello gets `features` (4-arg constructor kept); Msg.Delta; Protocol parses "delta" (same
  cycles/walls shape as state, plus seq/key/removed) and builds the host hello.
- BridgeClient: if the guest's hello offers "delta" (and -Darmacraft.delta is not false), send the host
  hello; fold each delta into a per-connection wall map on the bridge thread and publish a full
  Msg.State as before. The server thread is unchanged. Unchanged walls keep their record instances
  across snapshots, so 0002's memo hits on identity.
- Old guests never offer the feature -> nothing changes.

Effect: bridge-thread parse work becomes O(changed) (see docs/perf.md: Gson parse of a delta frame vs
a full frame). Bandwidth -74..76% (measured with 0003).
Checked: `git apply --check`; host main + test + gametest sources compile; host unit tests pass with
0002+0004 applied in a scratch copy; a scratch check fed delta lines through BridgeClient.handleLine
(keyframe, in-place head update, record identity kept, removed ids, keyframe replace, v1 state still
accepted). Not run against the patched guest end-to-end inside Minecraft.
Base: bridge/Msg.java, bridge/Protocol.java, bridge/BridgeClient.java as of 2026-10-02 00:01 BST.
Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/perf-patches/0004-proto-delta-host.patch

